#! /usr/bin/dh-exec
afirewall.conf etc/afirewall
# THE SAME FILE AGAIN, WHERE IT CANNOT BE EDITED. /etc/afirewall/afirewall.conf is a conffile and
# is meant to be changed - ansible composes a host's ruleset by enabling flags in it. That leaves
# nothing on the host stating what the defaults WERE, so a configuration manager that wants the
# end state to follow from what it just did has nothing to start from and can only accumulate.
#
# It is not "everything off": the defaults enable inbound.ssh and the outbound half a host needs to
# be administered, resolve, and update. A restore that guessed at that would close ssh.
afirewall.conf usr/share/afirewall
afirewall/afirewall.py => /usr/sbin/afirewall
lists etc/afirewall
templates etc/afirewall
